VERIFIED_THIS_PASS.update({
    "https://www.asam.net/standards/detail/xil/": "Inspected current ASAM XIL 3.0.0 standard page 2026-10-23. It defines a generic API between test automation and test benches and supports MIL/SIL/HIL, decoupling test cases from benches; v3.0.0 is explicitly not backward compatible with previous versions.",
    "https://www.asam.net/standards/detail/osi/": "Inspected ASAM OSI 3.8.0 page 2026-10-23. It defines simulator data-exchange interfaces including ground-truth, sensor-data, sensor-view and feature-data messages; it supports simulator/framework interoperability and does not itself validate ADS safety or fidelity.",
    "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43684-025-00112-1": "Inspected open-access 2025 survey on autonomous-driving risk assessment. The article surveys risk sources, methodologies and architectures; use as taxonomy/discovery, not primary validation of any one risk metric or safety case.",
    "https://engrxiv.org/preprint/view/7134": "Inspected 2026 EngrXiv preprint abstract on safety-critical ADS scenarios, benchmarks and verification pipelines. It proposes a taxonomy spanning geometry-based risk, learned anticipation, uncertainty-aware control and world-model/foundation-model approaches. It is a non-peer-reviewed preprint and abstract-level evidence only in this pass.",
    "https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware-documentation/latest/design/autoware-architecture/vehicle/": "Reopened Autoware Foundation Vehicle Interface design 2026-10-23. Confirms normalized command/status boundary, vehicle-specific translation to drive-by-wire, feature/diagnostic reporting, disengagement and manual override examples, and feedback outputs such as actuation state, odometry and control mode. Current maintained project documentation; not a safety certification or universal interface specification.",
    "https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware_universe/main/vehicle/autoware_raw_vehicle_cmd_converter/": "Inspected Autoware Raw Vehicle Command Converter docs 2026-10-23. Shows translation from trajectory/control outputs to platform actuator commands, steering gear-ratio conversion, feedback conversion and command-to-actuation latency measurement; the vehicle adaptor is explicitly marked under development. Stack- and vehicle-specific implementation, not a universal production recipe.",
    "https://github.com/ApolloAuto/apollo/blob/master/modules/common_msgs/external_command_msgs/chassis_command.proto": "Inspected Apollo ChassisCommand protobuf schema 2026-10-23. It carries command identity, standard vehicle signals and extensible custom operations. This is one software-stack message contract, not a cross-vendor standard or a complete E/E integration/safety design.",
    "https://www.itu.int/epublications/publication/itu-t-f-749-17-2025-12-functional-requirements-of-universal-interfaces-for-purpose-built-automated-driving-system-dedicated-vehicle": "Inspected ITU-T F.749.17 (12/2025), functional requirements for interfaces in purpose-built ADS-dedicated vehicles. The recommendation discusses modular/vehicle-agnostic interfaces, sensor/V2X/system interoperation, diagnostics and verification concepts. Its scoped recommendation and referenced standards do not establish general-purpose thresholds, regulatory adoption, or a universal interface for all vehicle types.",
})

