    {"source_id":"D011-BIRMINGHAM-FINANCIAL-ECONOMETRICS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"University of Birmingham, Birmingham Business School","title":"LM Financial Econometrics (2026/27 module description)","url":"https://program-and-modules-handbook.bham.ac.uk/webhandbooks/WebHandbooks-control-servlet?Action=getModuleDetailsList&pgCrse=36331&pgSubj=07&searchTerm=002026","source_family":"official university financial-econometrics curriculum","locator":"Official module search result for 2026/27 LM Financial Econometrics; direct page reopen returned 502. Description lists multivariate regression, MLE/moments/GMM, misspecification, measurement error/IV, DiD, RDD, financial time series/volatility, panel regression, event studies and qualitative-response models.","supports":"A finance-specific curriculum cross-check that treats financial econometrics as several methods chosen by data structure and question, not a single technique; shows both predictive/time-series and identification/empirical-design branches.","claim_limit":"One master's module and official search-result description, not a global consensus, proof all listed methods are compulsory, or universal prerequisite graph.","search_status":"official course search result inspected 2026-10-23; direct reopen 502"},
    {"source_id":"D011-YORK-FINANCIAL-ECONOMETRICS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"University of York","title":"Financial Econometrics (ECO00084M), 2026/27","url":"https://www.york.ac.uk/students/studying/manage/programmes/module-catalogue/module/ECO00084M/2026-27?creditLevel=&department=&electiveTheme=&isAvailableAsElective=false&isAvailableToVisitingStudents=true&max=15&offset=180&query=&teachingPeriod=","source_family":"official university financial-econometrics curriculum","locator":"Official 2026/27 module-catalogue search result; direct URL reopen returned a cache miss. Outcomes and content list regression assumptions, OLS/MLE/GMM, endogeneity, ARMA, unit roots/spurious regression, VAR/Granger/cointegration, GARCH, factor models, quantile/VaR and switching models.","supports":"Another finance-specific curriculum cross-check linking estimation/inference foundations to cross-section, time-series, volatility, asset-pricing and risk-model branches; emphasizes assumptions and technique selection for financial data.","claim_limit":"One university module and course description; establishes its instructional scope only, not universal use or exact role/route requirements. Software choice EViews is program-specific.","search_status":"official course result inspected 2026-10-23; direct reopen cache miss"},
    {"source_id":"D011-NHH-FINANCIAL-ECONOMETRICS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"NHH Norwegian School of Economics","title":"FIN538 Financial Econometrics (Autumn 2026)","url":"https://www.nhh.no/en/courses/financial-econometrics2/","source_family":"official university financial-econometrics curriculum","locator":"Official course page opened 2026-10-23; topics at lines 21â€“45; learning outcomes and access/prerequisites at lines 46â€“79. Page is for Autumn 2026, though its overview also displays an offering-status inconsistency; preserve the content/date and do not infer current enrollment availability.","supports":"Broad, explicit finance-method map covering OLS/MLE/GMM; panel/fixed-effects and time-series/volatility; causal designs IV/RDD/DiD/randomized/selection-on-observables; event studies, BHAR/CTAR, matching and Fama-MacBeth.","claim_limit":"Restricted advanced course with stated econometrics/asset-pricing prerequisites; course inclusion does not make every method compulsory for all roles or determine a fixed learner sequence.","search_status":"official course page opened 2026-10-23"},
