    {"source_id":"D011-R-CORRELATION-TESTS","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"R Core Team","title":"R stats: Pearson, Spearman and Kendall Correlation Tests","url":"https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/cor.test.html","source_family":"maintained statistical software documentation","locator":"R stats manual cor.test; opened 2026-10-23. Documents Pearson product-moment, Spearman rank and Kendall tau tests, their estimands, inference and exact/asymptotic options.","supports":"Official implementation-level comparison of correlation techniques and their alternatives, useful for finance data diagnostics, association analysis and signal screening where the task/source supports it.","claim_limit":"API documentation is not method-theory instruction or proof that any correlation is stable/predictive in financial data. Pearson and rank methods answer related but distinct association questions; sample dependence and time structure require separate treatment.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-R-CHI-SQUARE-TEST","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"R Core Team","title":"R stats: Pearson Chi-Squared Tests for Count Data","url":"https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/chisq.test.html","source_family":"maintained statistical software documentation","locator":"R stats manual chisq.test; opened 2026-10-23. Documents goodness-of-fit and contingency-table tests, expected counts, 2x2 continuity correction and Monte Carlo p-values.","supports":"Canonical procedure and implementation options for categorical/count-data inference that can be used in finance studies when the sampling design and expected-count conditions support the test.","claim_limit":"Chi-square is not a general-purpose numerical test or a substitute for regression; asymptotic validity and table design matter. It does not establish a finance-specific task route by itself.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-R-FISHER-EXACT-TEST","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"R Core Team","title":"R stats: Fisher's Exact Test for Count Data","url":"https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/fisher.test.html","source_family":"maintained statistical software documentation","locator":"R stats manual fisher.test; opened 2026-10-23. Documents conditional exact tests for contingency-table independence, exact/Monte Carlo options and limitations for larger tables.","supports":"A method alternative for suitable sparse contingency tables, enabling comparison with asymptotic Pearson chi-square inference under different count conditions.","claim_limit":"Fisher's exact test is conditional on fixed margins and can become computationally difficult for larger tables; it is not automatically preferable for every chi-square problem or every financial dataset.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-R-LM-ANOVA-ANCOVA","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"R Core Team","title":"R stats: Linear Models, Regression, ANOVA and ANCOVA","url":"https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/lm.html","source_family":"maintained statistical software documentation","locator":"R stats manual lm; opened 2026-10-23. Describes fitting linear models for regression, single-stratum ANOVA and ANCOVA, weighted fits and model contrasts; notes data/time-series alignment considerations.","supports":"Shows how regression and group-mean comparison procedures sit within a linear-model framework, including where weighted regression and time alignment require distinct choices.","claim_limit":"Software reference is not a complete inferential course. Correct use depends on design, dependence, error structure, coding and diagnostics; shared API does not make all procedures or results equivalent.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-R-GLM-BINARY-LOGISTIC","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"R Core Team","title":"R stats: Generalized Linear Models, Including Binomial/Logistic Regression","url":"https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/glm.html","source_family":"maintained statistical software documentation","locator":"R stats manual glm; opened 2026-10-23. Documents specifying response distribution and link, including binomial responses and iterative weighted least squares fitting.","supports":"Implementation reference for linking binary-outcome logistic regression to the broader generalized-linear-model family; clarifies that outcome scale and chosen link distinguish it from ordinary least-squares modeling.","claim_limit":"Does not teach full assumptions, separation, calibration, causal interpretation or market suitability. A binary outcome does not by itself prove logistic regression is the only suitable classifier.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
