    {"source_id":"D011-SCIKIT-MODEL-EVALUATION","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"scikit-learn project","title":"scikit-learn: Model Selection and Evaluation","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/model_selection.html","source_family":"maintained machine-learning software documentation","locator":"Official user guide; opened 2026-10-23. Covers cross-validation iterators, model/parameter selection, validation, and classification/regression scoring metrics.","supports":"Practical comparison/evaluation layer for traditional estimators and ML models; supports the general sequence from fitting to out-of-sample model selection and evaluation.","claim_limit":"General-purpose documentation does not establish leakage-safe evaluation for financial time series. Random folds can violate temporal information order; use time-aware splits and finance-specific validation evidence.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-SCIKIT-TIME-SERIES-SPLIT","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"scikit-learn project","title":"scikit-learn: Cross-Validation for Time-Series Data","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/cross_validation.html","source_family":"maintained machine-learning software documentation","locator":"Official cross-validation guide; opened 2026-10-23. Explains why ordinary KFold/ShuffleSplit i.i.d. assumptions can be inappropriate under temporal dependence and describes TimeSeriesSplit evaluating future observations; equal-interval and splitter limitations are stated.","supports":"Primary implementation guidance for preserving time order when comparing forecasting/ML models; identifies a concrete methodological difference from ordinary shuffled/random cross-validation.","claim_limit":"Generic TimeSeriesSplit is not sufficient for every financial label, overlapping horizon, panel or strategy backtest; PBO, purge/embargo and leakage controls need task-specific evaluation. Does not validate any return forecast.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-PBO-BACKTEST-OVERFIT-2017","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Journal of Computational Finance / UC eScholarship","title":"The Probability of Backtest Overfitting","url":"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/4w1110bb","source_family":"peer-reviewed quantitative-finance methodology research","locator":"Bailey, Borwein, LÃ³pez de Prado and Zhu (2017), Journal of Computational Finance 20(4), DOI 10.21314/jcf.2016.322; opened article record and paper. Defines PBO and combinatorially symmetric cross-validation for investment-strategy selection risk.","supports":"A finance-specific complement to ordinary predictive model evaluation: assessing whether the in-sample strategy configuration selected from many trials tends to underperform out-of-sample.","claim_limit":"Proposed framework with its own assumptions and use conditions; it does not replace forward holdout, economic transaction-cost analysis, or all other validation methods and is not a regulator requirement.","search_status":"published_article_record_and_paper_opened_2026-10-23"},
