    {"source_id":"D011-OPEN-GAMMA-RATES-CURVE-CALIBRATOR","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"OpenGamma Strata project","title":"RatesCurveCalibrator API","url":"https://strata.opengamma.io/apidocs/com/opengamma/strata/pricer/curve/RatesCurveCalibrator.html","source_family":"maintained open-source financial-pricing project documentation / credible grey literature","locator":"Strata API states curve calibration defines reference trades at curve nodes and prices/reprices them using a root finder to fit observed market quotes; supports curve groups, par-spread/present-value calibration measures and stores Jacobians in metadata.","supports":"Practical rate-curve calibration workflow, root-finding and calibration-measure choices for downstream instrument pricing and risk sensitivity.","claim_limit":"API describes Strata's implementation, not the only calibration approach or proof the market inputs/conventions are appropriate. Calibrating a curve to instruments is distinct from validating the resulting model or market-data quality.","search_status":"official OpenGamma Strata API documentation inspected 2026-10-23"},
